 "notes": "Wreck plan of the SS Carnatic (89.4 x 11.6 m) on the north face of Abu Nuhas, lying on its port side parallel to the reef, bow to the east, broken across the middle with the two halves settled close together. Position and reef edge from OpenStreetMap; dimensions and heading from Wikipedia and the Red Sea Wreck Project (18-27 m, three-bladed propeller at the stern); boiler, stern windows and the moray in the bow from first-hand observation. Feature depths are spread over the published range and the route and RIB drop are indicative; positions are approximate.",
